## Architectural Rules

- **All DB nutrient values are per 100g.** Scaling: `multiplier = grams / 100`.
- **Nutrition math is duplicated** in `backend/app/nutrition.py` ↔ `frontend/src/utils/nutrition.ts`. **Change BOTH.**
- **`calculate_recipe_macros` (backend, unused by any route)** returns a tuple: `(unrounded_per_serving: dict, rounded: MacroProfile)`. Frontend `calculateRecipeMacros` returns **unrounded** values only (no tuple) — FDA increment rounding is applied at presentation time by `formatNutrientAmount`/`formatDVFromAmount`, not in the calculation step. This is an **intentional divergence** from the backend's single-shot round-to-1-decimal (`round_half_up`), which is likewise no longer used for label display.
- **FDA increment rounding (21 CFR 101.9(c))** lives in `frontend/src/utils/nutrition.ts`: `formatNutrientAmount`, `formatTransFatAmount`, `formatAddedSugarsAmount`, `formatDVFromAmount` — each nutrient has its own increment (e.g. sodium rounds to nearest 5mg below 140mg, nearest 10mg above; micronutrient %DV uses coarser 2/5/10-point increments than macro %DV). `roundHalfUp`/`round1` still exist for simple half-up rounding (parity tests, non-label call sites) but are **not** how label values are formatted.
- **`labelSpec.ts`** (`frontend/src/components/label/`) is the single source of truth for the label's rows and geometry — both `LabelPreview` (DOM) and `LabelPdfDoc` (`@react-pdf/renderer`) consume `GEO`, `MACRO_ROWS`/`MICRO_ROWS`, and `rowDisplay()` so a value/rounding/%DV can never disagree between the on-screen preview and the downloaded PDF.
- **Search ranking**: prefix matches (`name_lower.startswith(q)`) before contains matches, alphabetical within each group; top **40** returned. No data-type tier (BM25 pre-filters 200).
- **DB is read-only at runtime** — SQLite URI `mode=ro&nolock=1`; writes happen only in `data/build_db_full.py`.
- **PDF generation is entirely client-side** (`@react-pdf/renderer`, lazy-imported on click by `GenerateButton` to keep it out of the initial bundle) — there is no PDF-generation network request, so no server-side SSRF guard, concurrency semaphore, or render timeout apply anymore.
- **Rate limits** (slowapi, per IP, env-configurable): search 60/min, food 120/min. 429 → JSON `detail` + `Retry-After` header. (The old `generate` 10/min limit was removed along with the route.)
- **savedRecipesStore**: max 50 recipes, max 20 versions each; `versions.at(-1)` = latest. v1→v2 migration wraps legacy flat snapshots as a single version.
- **`RecipeStep.text`** may contain `{Variable Label}` tokens parsed by `utils/stepText.ts`.
- **Frontend `baseMacros`** on `IngredientItem` is the raw per-100g API response — never scaled in store.
- **`portionRef`**: when set on `IngredientItem`, `amount` means "N portions"; `ingredientGrams()` honors this.
- **Per-row identity = `instanceId`** (Zustand-assigned UUID). Same `fdc_id` can appear twice as independent rows. **All `recipeStore` ingredient actions key off `instanceId`, not `fdc_id`.** Legacy persisted recipes get back-filled via `withInstanceIds`.
- **Unit swap preserves gram weight**: `updateIngredientUnit` re-expresses amount in new unit (100 g → 3.53 oz). Clears active `portionRef`. `updateIngredientPortion(null)` falls back to row's unit. Both round display amount to 2 decimals.
- **Label-meta overrides** (`recipeStore`, not derived from the USDA DB): `servingHousehold: string` (household serving description, e.g. "2/3 cup"), `addedSugarsG: number` (own %DV, DV 50g), `transFatG: number` (no %DV). `setAddedSugarsG`/`setTransFatG` clamp to `>= 0` and coerce `NaN` (e.g. a cleared input) to `0`; there is no upper clamp in the store (the `LabelDetails` UI caps the `ScrubNumber` input at 999). Persisted per-version in `RecipeVersion`/`RecipeSnapshot`; optional on `RecipeVersion` for backward compatibility with pre-existing saved versions (`stateFromVersion` defaults missing values to `""`/`0`).
- **CORS only enabled when `settings.cors_origins` is non-empty** (dev). In prod, nginx/Caddy proxies same-origin.
- **`TrustedHostMiddleware`** rejects requests whose Host header isn't in `allowed_hosts`.
- **`width_inches`/`height_inches` validation** (`MIN/MAX_WIDTH`/`MIN/MAX_HEIGHT` in `models.py`) is dead code now that `GenerateLabelRequest` has no route — the frontend's own dimension clamp (`useLabelResize`) is the only one that matters at runtime.
- **Schema divergence (intentional)**: backend `FoodSearchResult` includes `data_type: str | None`; frontend type omits it (unused on client).

